A stereo window on NVIDIA's own EGL is no longer black under Qt's own window frame (ORDER 146b). Qt takes an OpenGL ES config on NVIDIA's EGL, so the decorations context of a stereo window, which is desktop OpenGL (stereo3d-wayland-egl-eye-slots), could not be made from it ("Failed to create the decorations EGLContext") and the window stayed black wherever the compositor offers no server-side frame. The config chooser and q_glFormatFromConfig now allow desktop OpenGL for a stereo format on a display that lists EGL_EXT_multiview_window, which the gl-stereo layer gives over NVIDIA's EGL. NVIDIA's own EGL does not list it, so a program without the layer and every non-stereo format keep OpenGL ES as before (stereo3d-egl-desktop-gl-for-two-views-on-nvidia.patch).
